test interpret
test run
target scry32

; A signed maximum of unsigned-tagged inputs (`uext` parameters) whose
; result feeds a signed minimum. Both comparisons must be signed:
; smin(smax(-5, -13), 0) is -5, whereas comparing the intermediate
; 0xFFFFFFFB as unsigned against 0 would pick 0. The inputs cover both
; argument orders, all-positive values, and a mixed pair.

function %smax_smin(i32 uext, i32 uext) -> i32 uext {
block0(v0: i32, v1: i32):
    v2 = smax v0, v1
    v3 = iconst.i32 0
    v4 = smin v2, v3
    return v4
}
; run: %smax_smin(-5, -13) == -5
; run: %smax_smin(-13, -5) == -5
; run: %smax_smin(5, 13) == 0
; run: %smax_smin(-13, 5) == 0
